<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Fence installation in Dallas TX usually means one of two jobs: a new 6-ft or 8-ft wood privacy fence on a lot that never had one, or a full replacement of a fence that has leaned, greyed and lost pickets. This page covers how an installation runs from measuring to build, what the wood, post and style choices change on a quote, and what the City of Dallas says about height and permits. White Rock Fence Co is advertising that connects Dallas homeowners with independent fence contractors. It does not build fences itself.</p><p>Every price here is what one named firm publishes, or a national guide labeled as national. None of it is a quote from this site. Get two or three written quotes that list the same height, wood, posts and extras, then call (214) 555-0137 to be put in touch with an independent contractor who quotes the job.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Cedar or pine pickets</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">TX Fence & Deck lists 150 lf of pressure-treated pine at $2,200 to $3,300 installed and western red cedar at $3,000 to $4,500. Ask every quote to name the wood.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Side-by-side or board-on-board</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Board-on-board overlaps the pickets so the fence stays solid. TX Fence & Deck says it adds $2 to $5 per linear foot over a basic dog-ear fence.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Posts set in concrete</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Wood or steel posts, set in concrete, carry the fence. Much of the Dallas area sits on expansive clay, so ask what the quote specifies for posts.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Top cap and trim</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A cap and trim rail finish the top edge and shed water off the pickets. Check whether they are in the base price or priced as extras.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">City permit when height triggers one</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The City of Dallas requires a fence permit above 6 ft outside the front yard, and caps fences at 9 ft. Confirm with the City and your HOA before anything is built.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Tear-out and haul-off</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Taking down the old fence and hauling it away is its own line on a replacement quote. Ask whether it is included and who calls 811 before digging.</p>
      </div>
</div>
